{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","is_bot":false,"login":"konard","name":"Konstantin Diachenko"},"baseRefName":"main","body":"## Issue #131 - Translate punctuation, overrides, and article context\n\nFixes the Translate-page regression for:\n\n```text\nCalifornia (/ˌkælɪˈfɔːrniə/) is a state in the Western United States that lies on the Pacific Coast.\n```\n\n### Root cause\n\nThe issue combined several translation gaps:\n\n- punctuation/brackets and parenthesized IPA could enter lexical linking instead of remaining source text;\n- the n-gram gate split source-backed phrasal verbs such as `lies on`;\n- the Translate flow lacked a local source-backed override layer for missing or low-quality upstream data;\n- Russian target data and grammar forms were missing for `California`, `state`, `Western United States`, `Pacific Coast`, relative `that`, and geographic `lie on`;\n- linked article context was collected in the result but had no experimental recursive translation UI;\n- the JS semantic-lexicon changes needed the Rust mirror to stay in parity.\n\n### Fix\n\n- Preserves parenthesized pronunciation spans and excludes brackets from lexical phrase links.\n- Adds a default `virtual-source-overrides` tier with Links Notation rendering and semantic concept injection.\n- Adds source-backed override data for the issue sentence, including `lie on`, `that`, `California`, `state`, `Western United States`, and `Pacific Coast`.\n- Applies Russian naturalization rules for locative region case, relative `that`, prepositional objects, and sentence-level `then` punctuation.\n- Lets Translate resolve local semantic/virtual target labels before fetching target-language source data.\n- Adds experimental linked article context translation with summary fetching, bounded translation input, and cache keys that include source URL, target language, section, and revision.\n- Adds Translate UI controls for the virtual source and article-context experiment, plus linked article action buttons.\n- Mirrors the semantic-lexicon override merge, normalized glossary keys, and grammar-form lookup helpers in Rust.\n- Updates the issue #131 case study, generated formalize docs, changeset, and browser evidence.\n\n### Reproduction / verification\n\nThe reported sentence now translates to:\n\n```text\nКалифорния (/ˌkælɪˈfɔːrniə/) это штат на западе США, который расположен на Тихоокеанском побережье.\n```\n\nThe result has no unresolved translation questions. The regression test also covers parenthesis exclusion, `lying on` / `lies on` source-backed phrasal verb matching, virtual-source override link rendering, article-context caching, and Rust-side semantic override parity.\n\n### UI Evidence\n\n![Translate UI article context](https://github.com/link-assistant/meta-expression/blob/issue-131-84c06d630fcf/docs/case-studies/issue-131/data/translate-ui-article-context.png?raw=true)\n\n### Tests\n\n- `node --test js/tests/integration/issue-21-context-detection.test.js js/tests/integration/issue-56.test.js js/tests/integration/issue-96-paragraph-translation.test.js js/tests/integration/issue-131.test.js`\n- `npm test`\n- `npm run check`\n- `cargo test`\n- `node scripts/check-js-rust-parity.mjs --base origin/main`\n\nCloses #131.\n","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-05-31T23:40:33Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-05-31T23:40:33Z","messageBody":"Adding .gitkeep for PR creation (default mode).\nThis file will be removed when the task is complete.\n\nIssue: https://github.com/link-assistant/meta-expression/issues/131","messageHeadline":"Initial commit with task details","oid":"13c36686c6d21fdc95652a52f8d4000724435a59"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-01T00:19:08Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-01T00:19:08Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Fix issue 131 translation punctuation and phrasal verbs","oid":"7de9d7115545e8951cfd3ec69481a5e070e1b37c"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-01T00:19:19Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-01T00:19:19Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Document issue 131 case study","oid":"463817ed5db5c579141ab86c2c8e0f0fd41d609e"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-01T00:24:28Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-01T00:24:28Z","messageBody":"This reverts commit 13c36686c6d21fdc95652a52f8d4000724435a59.","messageHeadline":"Revert \"Initial commit with task details\"","oid":"7cac438cdd59a60205ea9b125cdac6bf3d63a704"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-01T11:00:58Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-01T11:00:58Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Complete issue 131 translate overrides and article context","oid":"46561c1ab5f4f87b4a217c612791d97b6ad441f9"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-01T11:09:32Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-01T11:09:32Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Mirror issue 131 lexicon overrides in Rust","oid":"c0f77af2cb86a1d2c2122d6f39e20a952c87ed39"}],"headRefName":"issue-131-84c06d630fcf","headRefOid":"c0f77af2cb86a1d2c2122d6f39e20a952c87ed39","isDraft":true,"number":132,"state":"OPEN","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-06-01T11:10:05Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/link-assistant/meta-expression/actions/runs/26751268693/job/78839580303","name":"Check Links","startedAt":"2026-06-01T11:09:55Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Broken Link Checker"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-06-01T11:09:59Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/link-assistant/meta-expression/actions